{"abstract":[{"text":"See what the server reports, and send it where you want it.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/Logging"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"NanoHTTP"}],"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Logging"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A server reports what nobody else can see: a handler that threw an error (with the method and path of the request), a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"response that could not be written, a pause in accepting connections, the connection limit, a response header that had to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be dropped, a WebSocket client that broke the protocol. The messages go to the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of the server’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"configuration, with a level: ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoLogLevel/debug","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoLogLevel/info","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoLogLevel/warning","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoLogLevel/error","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Level","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The server uses it for","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"a handler that threw an error other than ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; a response that could not be built, or whose body does not have the length that its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Content-Length","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" says","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"warning","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"a shortage that the server works around (out of file descriptors, the connection limit), a response header that was dropped","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"info","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"clients that went away or broke a protocol (a response that could not be written, a WebSocket frame that is not valid), a recovery","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"debug","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"nothing: it is for your own messages","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"anchor":"The-loggers-that-come-with-the-framework","level":3,"text":"The loggers that come with the framework","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default is a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoOSLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which writes to the unified logging system of Apple’s platforms: the messages appear in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the console of Xcode and in the Console app, with the subsystem ","type":"text"},{"code":"org.objecthub.NanoHTTP","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"command-line tool","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" does not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"see them in its terminal; it uses a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoConsoleLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which prints a line for every message. A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoSilentLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"discards everything.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let server = NanoHTTPServer()","server.configuration.logger = NanoConsoleLogger(minimumLevel: .info)   // [WARNING] Unable to accept a connection ...","try server.start(8080)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Set the logger before the server starts: a running server keeps the configuration it was started with.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Your-own-messages","level":3,"text":"Your own messages","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/log(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" logs with the logger of the server, from handlers and everywhere else, from any thread:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let server = NanoHTTPServer()","server.get[\"/order\"] = { request in","  server.log(.info, \"order from \\(request.address ?? \"unknown\")\")","  return .ok(.text(\"thanks\"))","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The message is an autoclosure: a logger that does not want the level does not build the text, so a ","type":"text"},{"code":".debug","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" message that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expensive to build costs nothing in a server that logs from ","type":"text"},{"code":".info","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Your-own-logger","level":3,"text":"Your own logger","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A logger is a type with one method. This one collects the lines for a window of an app (the iOS demo does the same):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["// file scope","/// Collects what the server reports.","final class ExampleOutputLogger: NanoHTTPLogger {","  private let lock = NSLock()","  private var lines = [String]()","","  func log(_ level: NanoLogLevel, _ message: @autoclosure () -> String) {","    guard level >= .info else {","      return","    }","    let line = \"\\(level): \\(message())\"","    lock.lock()","    lines.append(line)","    lock.unlock()","  }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A logger is called from the threads of the connections, also at the same time, so it must be safe for that. On a server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that runs on one thread (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/Threading-swift.enum/singleThread","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") it is called on that thread, and a logger","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that blocks (a slow disk, a network call) blocks the server: hand the line to another queue.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Coming-from-1x","level":3,"text":"Coming from 1.x","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NanoHTTPServerIO.log(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" was ","type":"text"},{"code":"open","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and printed to the console; subclasses overrode it to send the messages elsewhere. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"public","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" now (it logs at the level ","type":"text"},{"code":"info","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and the place to send messages elsewhere is the configuration’s logger. Code that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"overrides ","type":"text"},{"code":"log(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" no longer compiles, which is intended: the override would not see the messages of the server any more.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP":{"abstract":[{"text":"A small HTTP/1.1 server for apps and tools: routing, files, forms, uploads and WebSockets, without dependencies.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"NanoHTTP","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/HowARequestIsServed":{"abstract":[{"text":"Follow a request from the socket to your handler and back.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/HowARequestIsServed","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"How a Request Is Served","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/howarequestisserved"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/MiddlewareAndExtending":{"abstract":[{"text":"Look at every request before it is routed, and replace parts of the server by subclassing.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/MiddlewareAndExtending","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Middleware and Extending the Server","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/middlewareandextending"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoConsoleLogger":{"abstract":[{"text":"A logger that prints one line for every message, such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"[WARNING] Unable to accept a connection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", for command-line tools and for tests. By","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default the lines are printed to the standard output, and every line is flushed: when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the output goes to a pipe or a file (","type":"text"},{"code":"tool | tee log","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), the standard output is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"buffered, and the lines would otherwise show up late.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoConsoleLogger"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoConsoleLogger","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoConsoleLogger"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoConsoleLogger","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanoconsolelogger"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPConnection":{"abstract":[{"text":"A request that has been read from a connection, together with the handler that will","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"answer it. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/handle(connection:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" drives the connection with it:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"send(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes the response and returns the connection for the next request, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the connection has ended.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPConnection"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPConnection","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPConnection"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPConnection","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpconnection"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPDeferredResponse":{"abstract":[{"text":"The answer to a request that is sent later, from any thread.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPDeferredResponse"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPDeferredResponse","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPDeferredResponse"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPDeferredResponse","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpdeferredresponse"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPError":{"abstract":[{"text":"An error that a handler throws to answer a request with an error status code.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPError"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPError","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPError"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPError","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttperror"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPLogger":{"abstract":[{"text":"Receives the messages that a server reports: a response that could not be written, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pause in accepting connections, a handler that threw an error, a WebSocket client that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"broke the protocol. Set the logger of a server with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/logger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPLogger"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPLogger","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPLogger"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPLogger","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttplogger"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer":{"abstract":[{"text":"An HTTP/1.1 server with routing.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPServer"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPServer"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPServer","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserver"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO":{"abstract":[{"text":"The part of a server that deals with sockets and threads: it listens at a port,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepts connections, reads the requests of each connection on a thread of its own,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hands them to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/dispatch(request:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and writes the responses. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"builds routing on top of it; subclass this class to use the server without routing.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPServerIO"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoHTTPServerIO"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPServerIO","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/Threading-swift.enum/singleThread":{"abstract":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One thread does everything","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": it accepts connections, reads requests, calls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the middleware and the handlers, and writes the responses, one request at a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"time. Handlers, middleware and everything else that runs in them need no locks,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"because they never run at the same time. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/start(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" starts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that thread (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/acceptQoS","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is its priority); ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/run(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" uses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the calling thread.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"singleThread"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/Threading-swift.enum/singleThread","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"NanoHTTPServerIO.Configuration.Threading.singleThread","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/threading-swift.enum/singlethread"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/acceptQoS":{"abstract":[{"text":"The priority of the thread that accepts connections.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"acceptQoS"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@E@NSQualityOfService","text":"QualityOfService"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/acceptQoS","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"acceptQoS","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/acceptqos"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/logger":{"abstract":[{"text":"Receives what the server reports: a response that could not be written, a pause in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepting connections, a handler that threw an error, a WebSocket client that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"broke the protocol. The default is a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoOSLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which writes to the unified","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"logging system (the console of Xcode, the Console app). A command-line tool that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"should print to its terminal uses a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoConsoleLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoSilentLogger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"switches logging off.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"logger"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A10HTTPLoggerP","text":"NanoHTTPLogger"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/logger","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"logger","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/configuration-swift.struct/logger"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/dispatch(request:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Chooses the handler for a request and returns it with the variables that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request’s route defined (see ","type":"text"},{"code":"NanoHTTPRequest.params","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). The implementation of this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"class answers every request with ","type":"text"},{"code":"404 Not Found","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" overrides it to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"route, and sets ","type":"text"},{"code":"NanoHTTPRequest.rawParams","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the request, as the result has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"room for it.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dispatch"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"request"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A11HTTPRequestC","text":"NanoHTTPRequest"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> (["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A18HTTPRequestHandlera","text":"NanoHTTPRequestHandler"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/dispatch(request:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"dispatch(request:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/dispatch(request:)"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/handle(connection:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Serves a connection: calls the handler of its first request, sends the response and,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as long as the connection is kept alive, does the same for the following requests.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Returns when the connection has ended. Runs on the thread of the connection.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"handle"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"connection"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A14HTTPConnectionV","text":"NanoHTTPConnection"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/handle(connection:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"handle(connection:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/handle(connection:)"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/log(_:_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Logs a message with the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/logger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of the server. The server reports problems that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nobody else can see (a response that could not be written, a pause in accepting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connections, a response header that was dropped); your own code can use it too. May","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be called from any thread. The message is only built if the logger wants it.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"log"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A8LogLevelO","text":"NanoLogLevel"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@autoclosure"},{"kind":"text","text":" () -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/log(_:_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"log(_:_:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/log(_:_:)"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/logger":{"abstract":[{"text":"The logger of the server: the one of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/logger","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of the run that is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"going on, or, if the server is not running, the one that the next run will use.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"logger"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8NanoHTTP0A10HTTPLoggerP","text":"NanoHTTPLogger"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/logger","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"logger","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/logger"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/run(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Starts the server like ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/start(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", but accepts connections on the calling thread,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and returns only when the server has been stopped (with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/stop()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", from another","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"thread or a signal handler).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"run"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt16V","text":"UInt16"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/run(_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"run(_:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/run(_:)"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/start(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Starts to accept connections at ","type":"text"},{"code":"port","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" picks a free port, see ","type":"text"},{"code":"port()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns: the connections are accepted and served on threads of the server (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/Configuration-swift.struct/threading-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"). Does nothing if the server is already running or is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"being started or stopped by another thread.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"start"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt16V","text":"UInt16"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoHTTPServerIO/start(_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"start(_:)","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanohttpserverio/start(_:)"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoLogLevel":{"abstract":[{"text":"How important a message of the server is.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoLogLevel"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoLogLevel","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NanoLogLevel"}],"role":"symbol","title":"NanoLogLevel","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanologlevel"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoLogLevel/debug":{"abstract":[{"text":"Details that help to find out what happened: nothing the server reports by itself.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"debug"}],"identifier":"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoLogLevel/debug","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"NanoLogLevel.debug","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/nanohttp/nanologlevel/debug"},"doc://NanoHTTP/documentation/NanoHTTP/NanoLogLevel/error":{"abstract":[{"text":"A failure of the